  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Third prerelease. Nothing public is removed or changed since 0.2.0-alpha; the new API is added. New: ManiacMansion, a front door that opens a release from its folder (Open, then Play, Inspect or CreateEngine); GameInspector.Rooms, Scripts, Costumes and Palette; GameWorld.ReadAudio, SampleRate, ObjectsHere, ClickObject and Palette. Changed: only the English releases for the Commodore 64 and DOS are played, and others are refused with a NotSupportedException that names them; the 1987 and 1988 DOS demos now play; the inspector answers null, not an exception, for the index's empty slots and its entries that point at nothing. Fixed in all three releases, checked against ScummVM: a script that starts a cutscene goes on after it; left-facing figures are drawn in the right column; the 1987 release's messages have their proper colours. The maniacal tool has --help, --version, one-line errors and exit codes, and keeps each release's saves in a folder of its own: saves made before are in saves/maniac, to be moved by hand.",
